WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:00.875
(clapping)

00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:03.948
- So what did you wanna be
when you were a little kid?

00:00:03.948 --> 00:00:05.570
- Oh. (laughs)

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.278
I wanted to be alive and--

00:00:08.278 --> 00:00:09.362
(laughs)

00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:10.195
Not in jail.

00:00:10.195 --> 00:00:12.213
I grew up not under great circumstances.

00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:14.221
I grew up in the hood.

00:00:14.221 --> 00:00:16.460
I was surrounded by a lot
of violence, a lot of crime.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:17.580
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.190
- I was definitely a
product of my environment.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.023
- Yeah.

00:00:21.023 --> 00:00:22.130
- I kind of snapped out
of it when I was older,

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.750
when I realized it was
just kind of a dead road.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.693
My mum helped me.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.530
She sent me to live with my dad when I was

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.400
I think about 12, 13 when
I was bigger than her

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.100
and getting in tons of trouble.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:31.933
- Yeah.

00:00:31.933 --> 00:00:34.340
- So I really didn't honestly
know what I wanted to do

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.440
with my life, like for the rest of my life

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.460
till I was about 30 years old.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.520
And that's when I knew
that I wanted to be,

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.380
I wanted to entertain people.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:42.300
- That's so cool.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.900
And so cool to say and own

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.720
because a lot of people
give up on their dreams

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.210
'cause they think they've
aged out of whatever bracket

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.410
society tells you you're
supposed to be in.

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:52.060
And that's cool, like at 30 you were like,

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.010
I wanna do this.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.000
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.200
- My life started at 30.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.670
I wasted my twenties.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.360
I bounced at night clubs
from the time I was 17

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:00.193
till I was 30.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:01.026
- Wow!

00:01:01.026 --> 00:01:01.859
- Yeah, that's what I did.

00:01:01.859 --> 00:01:02.692
- Right on.

00:01:02.692 --> 00:01:04.535
And you're all gooshy, like
wishy little teddy bear.

00:01:04.535 --> 00:01:05.497
- I'm pretty gooshy.

00:01:05.497 --> 00:01:06.480
- And so great.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.400
Your mum is probably like wait, what?

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.350
From like your childhood.
- She was.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:10.960
Well even when I went into
professional wrestling,

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.100
because I was such an introverted kid,

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.030
she just like, that's you?

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.640
Speaking in front of thousands of people?

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.360
I can't believe it.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.546
But my mum is actually my
biggest fan like by far.

00:01:21.546 --> 00:01:22.846
- That's so cool.
- Yeah.

